          "api_error_status": null,
          "result": "**Recommendation: lead with the status, then show the reasons as two labeled, parallel rows under it.**\n\n- **Keep the top line simple.** The operator sees one status, \"Needs review\", with nothing else competing for attention. Reasons appear directly beneath it, never as a separate status.\n- **Label each reason by what the operator should do, not by its internal type.** \"Input may be wrong\" tells the operator to go verify the source data. \"Analysis did not finish\" tells them to rerun or wait. Avoid internal names like \"uncertain input\" or \"incomplete analysis\" in the UI.\n- **Put evidence one click or one expand away.** Each reason row shows a one-line summary of its strongest evidence inline, with full supporting detail collapsed below. This keeps the default view scannable and the detail available.\n- **Order by actionability when both appear.** Show the input reason first, because fixing input often makes the analysis reason moot. Say so in a short hint when both are present.\n- **Make the pair visually distinct but equal in weight.** Same row shape, same font, different icon. Neither should read as the \"real\" reason.\n\nRefinement question: when both reasons are present, should the operator be able to resolve them separately, or does the status clear only when both are resolved together?",
